COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: node /private/tmp/r13/final/ours-src/bin/<tool> -- lib/index.js; echo ---; git log --follow --format='%h %ad %an %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js | head -40
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short version:** Troy Goode created `lib/index.js` and still holds most of it. Douglas Christopher Wilson and a long tail of contributors added fixes along the way. The counts below come from surviving-lines, which uses `git blame`. I set aside the 2026-04-12 reformat commit (62628c0), which only changed whitespace and quotes. Without that correction, Troy holds 111 lines (51.9%).

**Who shaped it**

- **Troy Goode (2013–2016):** Wrote the original middleware and made most of the structural changes.
  - 2013: the first JSLint cleanups.
  - 2014: `Access-Control-Expose-Headers` support, Express 4 support (2.3.2), the fixes for #6, #19 and #20 (2.4.0), and the switch to the `vary` module.
  - 2015: the ESLint switch in #42.
  - 2016: 2.8.0 (#66, #73).
- **Contributors from 2014 to 2015:**
  - Shane Tomlinson normalized method names to uppercase.
  - Alberto Leal fixed `options.origin` callbacks being overridden.
  - Typicode added PATCH to the default methods.
  - Igor Soarez added `Vary: Origin` for specific origins.
  - Raymond Feng removed the closure in `applyHeaders`.
  - max.laverse added passing preflight requests on to `next()`.
  - DracoBlue added exposed headers to OPTIONS responses.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (May 2015):** Added RegExp and array support for `options.origin`. This was five commits, including one under the name `alex94puchades` with the same email address. Troy committed some of them, and surviving-lines credits the lines to Alejandro.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson (2017–2021):** Fixed several bugs.
  - Added `Vary: Access-Control-Request-Headers` for dynamic `allowedHeaders`.
  - Fixed a crash when an options delegate had no `methods` option.
  - Updated ESLint and made lint fixes.
- **Other 2016–2018 fixes:**
  - Hannah Wolfe named an anonymous middleware function.
  - Saad Tazi fixed a crash on frozen options.
  - Tomek Kopczuk added `Vary: Origin` for regular expressions.
  - Benjamin Eidelman worked around a Safari bug in the default preflight response.
  - Tom Arad fixed `maxAge` set to 0.
  - Chima Alaebo removed an unreachable branch.
- **2021 and 2026:** LuisEGR removed unused parameters in a lint fix, which Douglas committed. Troy came back on 2026-04-10 with "annotate handlers", then the formatter commit landed.

**Whose code is still there** (214 non-blank lines, 238 counting blank lines, 62 commits)

| Author | Lines | Share | Lines with blank | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (<email redacted>) | 132 | 61.7% | 147 | 61.8% | 2019-05-27 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 9.3% | 22 | 9.2% | 2021-09-07 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 | 6.5% | 16 | 6.7% | 2015-05-28 |
| Troy Goode (troy@laptop.example) | 12 | 5.6% | 12 | 5.0% | 2026-04-10 |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.8% | 6 | 2.5% | 2021-07-20 |
| Raymond Feng | 6 | 2.8% | 7 | 2.9% | 2015-01-13 |
| max.laverse | 5 | 2.3% | 6 | 2.5% | 2015-04-15 |

- **Everyone else:** 15 more authors hold 5.1% together, and the largest of them is Mathias Buus at 0.9%.
- **One person or two:** The two Troy Goode rows probably belong to the same person, since the name matches. If so, Troy holds 144 lines (67.3%). I haven't merged them, and only you can confirm it is one person. The Alejandro and `alex94puchades` rows are already counted as one because they share an address.
- **Bus factor:** It is 1, because Troy alone holds over 50%. Only one of the 18 authors has committed in the last 365 days, and that is Troy, who holds 67.3% of the lines if the two rows are one person. The other 32.7% belongs to people with no commit in that time, including Douglas, who holds 9.3%.
- **Not set aside:** fcd2b56 ("switch to ESLint; clean up") looks mechanical and I did not set it aside. It accounts for 5 surviving lines.

These figures measure which lines survive, not the quality of the work or who reviewed or designed it. They also don't show code that was deleted on purpose.

