## 🔍 Code History: `lib/index.js`

### Quick Context
> This is the core of the `cors` Express/Connect middleware. It decides which CORS headers to send and handles preflight `OPTIONS` requests. Troy Goode wrote it in 2013, and he still owns most of the surviving lines. Doug Wilson later took over maintenance and hardened it.

### Decision Timeline
| Date | Commit | Author | What and why |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2013-01-30 | `bcd03d9` and the next few | Troy Goode | First commit, then case-insensitive header lookup, `origin: false` disabling CORS, and lint cleanup. |
| 2013-02 to 03 | `ed5128c`, `e572aa6`, `b093d7e` | Troy Goode, Damien Klinnert | Pause/resume of the request for async middleware. After a closer read of the CORS spec, most headers were limited to preflight responses. |
| 2013-04 to 05 | `7bb0686`, `e4ad50b`, `58562c8` | Simon Mansfield | Credentials-header placement and guards for a missing `Origin` header. |
| 2013-10 | `a8f9fdb`, `580c249`, `9a1b6e4` | Eric di Domenico, Mathias Buus, Troy Goode | `origin` can be a callback. Express-only request/response methods were replaced so Connect works without Express (v2.1.0). |
| 2014 | `0a80d70`, `e4afa9e`, `c78ed42` | Troy Goode, Typicode | `Access-Control-Expose-Headers`, `PATCH` added to the default methods, and Express 4 support. |
| 2014-10 to 11 | `37ca05d`, `165f35e`, `fee800f` | Igor Soarez, Troy Goode | `Vary: Origin` for specific origins, then moved to the `vary` module. A regression that dropped non-Express support was fixed. |
| 2015 | `39c9f29` to `e64e854` and others | Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (as `alex94puchades` on `39c9f29`), Raymond Feng, others | RegExp and array `origin` matching, `applyHeaders` optimized, preflight passthrough via `next()`, and the move to ESLint. |
| 2016 to 2017 | `5dae6d8`, `e0115b0`, `6d2ff29`, `075c4b5`, `d3304ab` | Troy Goode, Saad Tazi, Tomek Kopczuk, Doug Wilson, Benjamin Eidelman | Fixes for frozen options and `Vary` correctness. A Safari workaround was added for the default preflight response. |
| 2018 to 2021 | `01477dc`, `f038e77` | Tom Arad, LuisEGR | `maxAge: 0` fix and lint cleanup. |
| 2026-04 | `b2005d9`, `62628c0` | Troy Goode, Fiona Formatter | "Annotate handlers" (12 lines changed), then a whole-file reformat to 4-space indent and double quotes. |

### Narrative
The file grew by accretion. Each phase came from a bug report or a spec detail: async middleware, the Connect/Express split, then `Vary` handling. After 2017 almost all changes were small correctness fixes or lint changes. Doug Wilson authored most of these; he is the second-largest contributor to the surviving lines.

The two newest commits change how the blame output reads. `62628c0` is a pure style reformat. A plain blame credits Fiona Formatter with 32 lines that she didn't write the logic for. I ran blame with `-w -C -C -C` and with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`, so the second table is the real picture.

**Whose code is still there** (line counts from blame, ignoring the reformat):

